        You will be given the root cause of a bug, the commit message and the corresponding patch.
        You need to extract all code statements that lead to the bug from the patch, based on the root cause and the commit message.

        Root cause:
        The bug was caused by the `compare` method in the `LiteWorkflowInstance` class attempting to compare two `Date` objects that were initialized to `null` instead of a valid date. This resulted in a Null Pointer Exception (NPE) when the method tried to call `compareTo` on a `null` value, particularly during a rerun of workflows that involve forks, where action end times may not be set.

        Commit message:
        OOZIE-1989 NPE during a rerun with forks (rkanter)  

        Patch:

         @Override
         public int compare(String node1, String node2) {
-            Date date1 = FAR_INTO_THE_FUTURE;
-            Date date2 = FAR_INTO_THE_FUTURE;
+            Date date1 = null;
+            Date date2 = null;
             NodeInstance node1Instance = executionPaths.get(node1);
             if (node1Instance != null) {
                 date1 = this.actionEndTimes.get(node1Instance.nodeName);
             }
             NodeInstance node2Instance = executionPaths.get(node2);
             if (node2Instance != null) {
                 date2 = this.actionEndTimes.get(node2Instance.nodeName);
             }
+            date1 = (date1 == null) ? FAR_INTO_THE_FUTURE : date1;
+            date2 = (date2 == null) ? FAR_INTO_THE_FUTURE : date2;
             return date1.compareTo(date2);
         }



        Provide a response strictly in the following format:
        Code statements:
        <text1>
        <text2>
        ...
        <textN>

Code statements:
```java
Date date1 = null;
Date date2 = null;
date1 = (date1 == null) ? FAR_INTO_THE_FUTURE : date1;
date2 = (date2 == null) ? FAR_INTO_THE_FUTURE : date2;
return date1.compareTo(date2);
```

Code statements:
```java
Date date1 = null;
Date date2 = null;
return date1.compareTo(date2);
```
